    "id": "tool:check-against-a-persons-rules-and-verdicts",
    "label": "Check words or anything made against a person's own rules and verdicts",
    "status": "active",
    "job": "Check words, a title, a script line or a plan against a person's own rules and the verdicts they already gave, and say pass, fail or uncertain for each, with why",
    "description": "Give the units to check (each { text, kind } or { view, kind } for JSON such as a plan, with optional facts, field, context and findings you already have), rules (rule rows judge-words runs, and ask rows a model answers), and the person's own rule document (verdict_rules) and stands (stances, as tool:read-where-you-stand gives them), read at run time from their records or files. Or give a branch in place of rules and verdict_rules: one of the person's method rows (list:methods, such as the kind of thing being made: a book, a script, an article, a post), and the rules are read from their own records: the rows of their one Checks list (list:checks) whose method is that branch or a branch it extends, each branch read on its own, plus the rows of every list a branch names in check_lists; step rows (questions of a decision step) and rows set Off are left out, and a row that states no test (no words, pattern, exact, check, groups, path, evidence, ask or part, or a piece of a source file) is never judged: it is counted in rows_used.skipped.no_test and listed in read_by_a_model for a model to read, and a branch with only such rows answers no-applicable-rule; and the rows of the nearest branch carrying judge_settings (and of the branches extending it) are their verdict rows under those settings, the inherited rows generic rules. The answer then adds branch, lineage (nearest first) and rows_used. Their exact stand on a thing decides first: disagree fails, partly holds at review and fails at final, agree passes and clears the generic rules they named. Then their stated rows fail and their inferred rows (at_most uncertain) only hold. Nothing passes on silence: a thing nothing of theirs judges is novel, and an ask row never passes without a calibrated answer. The answer lists the questions a model may answer, by id; send the answers back in answers to use them. Nothing about any person is built in.",
    "input_schema": {
     "type": "object",
     "required": [
      "units"
     ],
     "anyOf": [
      {
       "required": [
        "rules"
       ],
       "not": {
